e conclude that the line $y=\\frac{6}{5}x+3$ is perpendicular to the given line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514739 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a9febaa-84c1-5184-96f6-09b381c7ca95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514711} {:answer/id #uuid "402a1ca3-e9dc-560b-bca6-a8ff47d34ff0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{8}{9}x+11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514713} {:answer/id #uuid "5b2560d4-42ed-589b-a70f-98b751d9ac0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{9}{8}x+12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514716} {:answer/id #uuid "6a835dc6-15d6-5d82-a0d5-319758a7aa80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{9}{8}x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514719} {:answer/id #uuid "acac5399-3f1f-5234-b5c8-c4e5c48aeb64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{8}{9}x-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acac5399-3f1f-5234-b5c8-c4e5c48aeb64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{8}{9}x-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514737} :answer-field/id #uuid "716c6c26-c7bd-51ed-93a0-38f6dced205b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514721}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c80adf7e-47a6-54d1-b617-5172bdeee1f4" :question/problem "Which of the following lines is perpendicular to $-18x-16y=18?$" :question/worked-solution "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\nTo find the slope of the given line $-18x-16y=18,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-18x-16y & =18 \\\\ -16y & =18x+18 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{18}{16}x-\\frac{18}{16} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{9}{8}x-\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope of the given line is $-\\frac{9}{8}.$\n\nLooking at the answer choices, the line $y=\\frac{8}{9}x-7$ has a slope of $\\frac{8}{9}.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{9}{8})\\cdot \\frac{8}{9}=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the slopes multiply to $-1,$ we conclude that the line $y=\\frac{8}{9}x-7$ is perpendicular to the given line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "560b5f98-cb98-58a6-98b4-bf241dfb030a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{5}{8}x+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514715} {:answer/id #uuid "6064a7af-8df0-5dd7-9b0e-33bb9fa615e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{8}{5}x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514718} {:answer/id #uuid "6f7ecb44-1bd3-5e97-9d1c-5e976e1bf5e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{8}{5}x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514720} {:answer/id #uuid "88aaa3a6-b77c-5219-8e9f-dd2ee93a12ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{5}{8}x+11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514730} {:answer/id #uuid "8f5c6db8-ea53-53f9-9e4f-5a841e917fdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6064a7af-8df0-5dd7-9b0e-33bb9fa615e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{8}{5}x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514718} :answer-field/id #uuid "11304265-79eb-53d3-b36a-ddf025ee509b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514704}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d4a46443-67d5-52dc-a8f6-c15f53d72a9b" :question/problem "Which of the following lines is perpendicular to $-10x+16y=-4?$" :question/worked-solution "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\nTo find the slope of the given line $-10x+16y=-4,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10x+16y & =-4 \\\\ 16y & =10x-4 \\\\ y & =\\frac{10}{16}x-\\frac{4}{16} \\\\ y & =\\frac{5}{8}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope of the given line is $\\frac{5}{8}.$\n\nLooking at the answer choices, the line $y=-\\frac{8}{5}x+3$ has a slope of $-\\frac{8}{5}.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot (-\\frac{8}{5})=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the slopes multiply to $-1,$ we conclude that the line $y=-\\frac{8}{5}x+3$ is perpendicular to the given line."}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Lines in Standard Form are Perpendicular"}]}
